WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.592 --> 00:00:02.170
(upbeat bright music)

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:07.170
- I'm gonna take us to
the first place I lived

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.057
until I was seven years old.

00:00:10.057 --> 00:00:12.630
(upbeat bright music)

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.680
Hang on to your hats.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.890
I kinda thought about this
was to just basically do this

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.613
in chronological order.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:28.690
So this was my street
back in the seventies.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:32.830
This neighborhood wasn't super savory.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:33.720
This is it.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.510
It looks so much nicer, by the way,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.108
with like the greenery and the gate.

00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:42.275
(upbeat bright music)

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:52.990
They really made it look
so much more romantic.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.420
The bars were on the windows

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.090
because it just wasn't safe enough,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.720
but the neighborhood has
gotten so much better.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.203
It was pretty scary when I was a kid here.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.763
God, I'm so tempted to
just beg them to let me in.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.923
A dinger, a doorbell.

00:01:14.361 --> 00:01:17.611
(dramatic piano music)

00:01:21.612 --> 00:01:25.383
I don't have to be lonely anymore.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.313
I was so lonely in this house.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:30.970
It was just me and my mom,

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:35.550
and it was just a really sad energy.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.713
It was very empty and very lonely.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.940
And you know, I grew up and got
in charge of my own destiny.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.130
And now my house is like
Grand Central Station.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:51.653
There's so much life and
there's so many people.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.650
And this place just taught me

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.310
that I wasn't the kind of
person who wanted to live

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:04.310
in a quiet lonely place.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.960
I wanted to live a life where
I was around a lot of people,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.740
but they've made the outside so pretty.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.500
It's like, it's not dark at all.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.240
It's very blooming and I
see little limes growing

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.580
and hummingbird feeders.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.963
It has a real sweetness now.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.357
And 10.

00:02:24.357 --> 00:02:27.274
(quirky fun music)

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.485
Are you manning that thing?

00:02:37.485 --> 00:02:39.814
- Yeah, we're doing software testing.

00:02:39.814 --> 00:02:42.506
- You're doing software testing?

00:02:42.506 --> 00:02:44.783
Well, there's a full circle future moment.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:49.020
Do you live here?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.930
I can't believe you're here.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.670
- [Owner] I can't believe you're here.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.400
- Well, I just so wanted
to revisit this place.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.900
This place means so much to me.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.920
I spent zero months to seven years old.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.620
Could I please just walk around the back?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.159
I'll walk, do one loop and leave.

00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:06.010
- [Owner] Okay. Okay.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.100
- Thank you so much.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.420
We'll leave everybody outside.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.143
Thank you for this opportunity.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:12.636
- [Owner] Come back anytime.

00:03:12.636 --> 00:03:14.210
- Okay, I'll come visit.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.380
I come to LA quite a bit.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.060
If there was one thing I learned here,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.913
my mom used to, whenever we would eat,

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.450
she would like stand up at the counter

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.370
and I would eat at the table,

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.230
but I was like, why can't we sit down

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.710
and have a meal together?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.350
And I judged her for it.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.890
And I just felt like,
why can't we sit down

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:42.090
and have like proper family dinners?

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:44.360
And it's so funny 'cause I'm a single mom

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.055
running around my kitchen with my kids,

00:03:46.055 --> 00:03:48.060
and I have them sitting at the counter

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.390
and I'm running around and
I'm like, oh, I get it.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.010
It's hard.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:58.010
You know, to live up to that
Norman Rockwell fantasy.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.070
It's so not real life.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.623
Yeah, I get it now for sure.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.360
I've learned so much living in this place,

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.900
and I thank you for keeping it beautiful.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.693
Making it more beautiful.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.423
Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:04:14.418 --> 00:04:16.368
(sirens wailing)

00:04:16.368 --> 00:04:18.118
Oh shoot. Is that me?

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.470
I used to get pulled over all the time

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.633
so every time I hear a
siren I'm like, oh it's me.

00:04:25.633 --> 00:04:30.633
I learned to drive at Sophia
Loren's ranch in Calabasas.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.750
Her two sons Carlo and Eduardo taught me

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.243
in a Renault Le Car, and they
taught me on a stick shift.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:48.853
This is it.

00:04:50.279 --> 00:04:51.112
Oh my God.

00:04:51.112 --> 00:04:53.500
When I was trying to
attempt sleeping at night,

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.300
even though I was just so scared,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.280
this is what cats sound
like when they are mating.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.123
Are you ready?

00:05:03.644 --> 00:05:07.311
(Drew imitates cat wailing)

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.163
That was the soundtrack to this apartment.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.670
Back in the 70s, this neighborhood

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.660
wasn't super savory.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:23.143
I mean, for a 14 year old,
I was like, I was scared.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:29.273
And I'm not scared anymore.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.433
I'm not scared anymore at all.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.880
But I'm so happy that this 14
year old girl is totally okay.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.750
And it hasn't been okay the whole time.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:49.770
Even a few years ago, getting
divorced, I felt so broken.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.360
I think the most broken
I've ever felt in my life

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:56.130
because all of a sudden it
wasn't about me anymore.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.010
It was about two people I cared about

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.760
much more than myself.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.700
That's real fear.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:06.600
That's bigger fear than
anything I experienced as a kid.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:11.600
I definitely am glad that
my kids, no matter what,

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.810
'cause we're gonna, all of
us are gonna screw it up

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:15.643
with our kids.

00:06:15.643 --> 00:06:18.950
We're gonna do our best, but
we're gonna make mistakes.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:22.160
I'm so glad that my kids won't be having

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.433
to live on their own at 14.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:30.683
And that's as healing to the
14 year old me as it can get.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:37.430
It's nice for just a moment
to think everything's okay.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.130
It will disappear later this afternoon

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.240
or tomorrow the next day,

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:42.840
and you have to fight for it to come back.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:47.840
But, in this moment, I
felt really relieved.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.280
By the way, that's an
underrated emotion, relief.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:54.960
(upbeat bright music)

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.490
I feel is that we might have to like stop

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:00.090
at a Poquito Mas today.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:03.130
I love California Mexican food.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:07.933
That California soft fluffy
rice and those refried beans.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.290
There's nothing like it.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:16.730
So this is Book Soup,
which was a bookstore

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.550
that I used to go to when I was a kid

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:23.810
because when I was 14 and living
on my own and emancipated,

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.110
the judge was like, by the way,

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.970
you never have to go to school again.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:30.371
And I was like, yes!

00:07:30.371 --> 00:07:31.710
Peace!

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.570
I'm never going to school again.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.170
And then I was like, oh my God,

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:38.340
I don't want to be uneducated.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:42.440
So I hit the books and this was honestly

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:43.673
my favorite bookstore.

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.210
I would always look for the classics.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:52.920
I would start with A,
and then I spent 25 years

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.493
trying to make it to Z.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.060
I started to think for a while

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:05.210
that unless a book was this thick,

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.023
that it wasn't gonna be for me.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.903
Here is John Fante.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:14.360
I've read every book he's ever written.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:19.200
The same with Joan Didion
and Charles Bukowski.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.900
Funny thing is is no
matter how much you read,

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.490
no matter how much you try,

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:28.650
you will never ever read everything.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.230
You'll never get there.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.770
There's not one Kurt Vonnegut
book that I've ever read

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.258
that I didn't put down and think,

00:08:35.258 --> 00:08:39.730
I just got to live in
the mind of a mad genius

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.630
that made my life better.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:44.727
And I actually got to have
dinner with him one night,

00:08:44.727 --> 00:08:48.900
and he ate baked beans and drank vodka.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.183
And it was the most amazing night ever.

00:08:54.559 --> 00:08:56.309
This is my favorite book right now.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.743
The best ever.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:05.460
Do yourself a favor and read
everything she's ever written.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.060
It's the one thing I'm
not willing to share.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.960
You can have the shirt off my
back and the keys to my car,

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.663
but if you touch my book, I will end you.

00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:19.806
(upbeat Latin fusion music)

00:09:23.087 --> 00:09:23.920
Mm.

00:09:25.871 --> 00:09:26.704
Mm.

00:09:28.117 --> 00:09:28.950
Mm.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.220
Okay, this is the area
that the laundry mat was.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.986
I mean, everything is so different now.

00:09:37.986 --> 00:09:39.440
(Drew gasps)

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:40.273
This is it.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:43.630
Oh my God. It's still here.

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:44.963
The Washing Machine.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:50.030
This is such a dream to be here.

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.800
I spent years here.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.710
When I first lived in my
apartment that I was so scared in,

00:09:55.710 --> 00:10:00.190
the truth was is that I would
let the laundry and dishes

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.110
and everything pile up.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.674
I didn't know how to clean.

00:10:02.674 --> 00:10:07.674
But this was where I learned
how to take care of myself.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.780
You know, the books were the school,

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.400
and this was like the domestic journey

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.860
of learning how to live on your own.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.360
Kids don't know how to
take care of themselves

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.693
until you teach them.

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:23.273
Olive and Frankie I'm coming for you.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:25.663
This was my row.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:31.510
And I would open and I
would stew in the bleach

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:35.570
like I was a witch at her cauldron.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:38.840
Like I was butter churning that stuff.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.007
(upbeat bright music)

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.603
This is the origins of
my stain removal story.

00:10:47.735 --> 00:10:51.550
(upbeat bright music)

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:55.480
Everything was okay inside of this temple.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.580
If there's one corner in Los Angeles

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.130
that I might love the most,

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:03.660
it might be right here on the
corner of Sweetser and third.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.000
Hey, it has the word sweet in it.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.510
And I just take these
lessons and these feelings

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:13.050
and they're still as relevant to me today

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:14.760
as they have ever been.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:17.174
That we can just take some time out,

00:11:17.174 --> 00:11:20.950
and we can clean up our
lives, our side of the street,

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.920
our laundry, our behavior, everything.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:27.310
Just purify it somehow.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.150
Clean it.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:29.760
It doesn't have to be perfect.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:32.070
It doesn't erase anything.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.077
Although I will erase the stain.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:38.830
I can't erase my life's
problems and nor do I want to,

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:40.380
but stains they have got to go.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:44.393
This right here.

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:47.825
The place was called the Barb Wire.

00:11:47.825 --> 00:11:52.825
Yeah, that's it.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.322
Nobody's answering.

00:11:58.322 --> 00:12:01.489
(soft dramatic music)

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.810
I was a real wild child.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.960
And I just got so out of control

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:19.633
that no one knew what to do with me.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:24.080
And so my mom called a friend

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:26.050
because her daughter was out of control

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:30.370
and they drove me here in
the middle of the night,

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:33.410
and they walked me right
through those two doors.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.850
And when you go through those two doors,

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.213
you do not come out.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.193
And I was there for a year and a half.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:46.783
And

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.150
I hated it.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.460
I kicked. I screamed.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.567
One minute, you're at movie
premieres and clubbing,

00:12:54.567 --> 00:12:58.390
and the next minute you're
in a full blown institution

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:01.623
with barbed wire everywhere,
and you can't get out.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:06.880
I think this is important
for me to share with people

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:09.010
because when they watch our show,

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.763
we have a very beautiful set.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.440
And I get to dress in nice clothing

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.230
and get my hair and makeup done.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.823
And there's an elegance
hopefully to the show,

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.830
but I will never lose sight
of this part of my story.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:33.070
And I have seen and been through things,

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.640
and they've helped me

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:40.520
just recognize in all of us

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:44.930
that we go through stuff and
it can't be embarrassing.

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.703
It has to be our strengths.

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:49.940
It has to be something
that we can be proud of

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.160
because we overcame it

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:56.160
and we look back with
honor and humor. (chuckles)

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:03.400
Life is so wonderful compared
to what it was in this place.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:08.400
I can't even believe I actually
get to be where I am now

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.680
because when I was
here, I didn't see that.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.410
I thought I would be here forever.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:17.500
I never thought I was gonna
make it to somewhere better.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.983
And I'm just so happy with my life.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:25.030
And I don't know if I
would have the life I have

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.093
if it wasn't for a place like this.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:33.240
So it was so important to come here today

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.703
and just like honor this.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:42.430
I think this can be a good
gateway to start season two

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.570
and go deeper with people.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.800
I'm never gonna not wanna be funny.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.500
I'm never gonna not wanna play.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.330
I'm never gonna not wanna be positive

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.860
and find the good stuff,

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.750
but I've seen some stuff and we all have,

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:56.890
and we need to deal with it.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:15:01.890
And we need to figure
out how to fix ourselves

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.023
and work on ourselves.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:06.313
It's very empowering.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.933
It's very celebratory.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.150
I wouldn't wanna go back.

00:15:14.150 --> 00:15:17.330
I just get to visit it in
my dreams and wave hello

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.273
and no, I'm not here anymore.

00:15:20.283 --> 00:15:21.463
And that's pretty cool.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:26.880
Welcome to the "Drew
Barrymore Show." (laughs)

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.703
Where we like to keep it real.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:39.237
(upbeat bright music)

